# Keep the Docker build context lean. Without this file, the 1.5 GB
# Imagenette training set under src/imagenette2/ and the multi-hundred-KB
# damage_report.png visualizer output get copied into the build context
# on every `til build noise`, blowing up image size and push time.
#
# Runtime artefacts inside the image (kept):
#   - src/advgan.py                — Generator architecture
#   - src/advgan_generator.pth     — trained generator weights (~14 KB)
#   - src/noise_manager.py         — inference path
#   - src/noise_server.py          — HTTP wrapper
#
# Everything below is training-side or analysis-only and stays on the
# Workbench disk.

src/imagenette2/
src/damage_report.png
src/train_advgan.py
src/simulate_damage.py
src/data/

# Python build noise.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
